@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-8c-spreading`

-- Tests for s 8(c) (spreading). Expected values were worked by hand from the section before they were run. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- The window of "six tax years ending in the year received": for a receipt in 2026, 2021 to 2026. All amounts are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 8(c)`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A difference of wages or of an annuity`
`a difference relating to` y `of` a MEANS
    `A difference of wages or of an annuity` WITH
        `the tax year the difference relates to` IS y
        `the amount of the difference`           IS a

GIVEN ds IS A LIST OF `A difference of wages or of an annuity`
GIVETH AN `Income to be spread under section 8(c)`
`the differences:` ds MEANS `wage differences or annuity differences` ds

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
      w IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income to be spread under section 8(c)`
`vacation pay of` a `over` n `years, the employee having worked` w `years` MEANS `vacation redemption pay received by an employee` a n w

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      ys IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income to be spread under section 8(c)`
`a grant of` a `for the working years` ys MEANS
    `a grant or a commutation of an annuity of paragraph (5) or (6) of the definition of income from personal exertion` a ys NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      ys IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      ds IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income to be spread under section 8(c)`
`a grant of` a `for the working years` ys `with a period allowed by the Director of` ds MEANS
    `a grant or a commutation of an annuity of paragraph (5) or (6) of the definition of income from personal exertion` a ys (JUST ds)

`the default older reading` MEANS `declined where the place of an older difference changes the answer`
`the default working-years reading` MEANS `declined where the working years outside the six tax years change the answer`

§§ `Paragraph (1): differences in the years they relate to`
-- Received in 2026: 2024 10,000 ; 2022 6,000 ; 2025 4,000 each stay in the year they relate to (all inside 2021 to 2026).
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`the differences:` (LIST `a difference relating to` 2024 `of` 10_000, `a difference relating to` 2022 `of` 6_000, `a difference relating to` 2025 `of` 4_000)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2024 `of` 10_000, `a share in the tax year` 2022 `of` 6_000, `a share in the tax year` 2025 `of` 4_000
-- 2021 is the earliest of the six: stays in 2021.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`the differences:` (LIST `a difference relating to` 2021 `of` 3_000)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2021 `of` 3_000
-- 2020 is older than the six: placed in the year of receipt, or in 2021 (the earliest of the six), or declined.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`the differences:` (LIST `a difference relating to` 2020 `of` 3_000)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `an older difference is placed in the year of receipt` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2026 `of` 3_000
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`the differences:` (LIST `a difference relating to` 2020 `of` 3_000)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `an older difference is placed in the earliest of the six tax years` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2021 `of` 3_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`the differences:` (LIST `a difference relating to` 2020 `of` 3_000)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` BECAUSE "section 8(c)(1) does not say where a difference older than the six tax years is placed, and here the place changes the answer"
-- No request: not open.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`the differences:` (LIST `a difference relating to` 2024 `of` 10_000)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` FALSE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` BECAUSE "section 8(c) regards the income as received in other years only at the request of the assessee or the heirs"

§§ `Paragraph (2): vacation redemption pay in equal annual parts`
-- 60,000 over 3 years, received in 2026: 20,000 in each of 2024, 2025, 2026.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`vacation pay of` 60_000 `over` 3 `years, the employee having worked` 10 `years`) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2024 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2025 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2026 `of` 20_000
-- Over 6 years: 10,000 in each of 2021 to 2026.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`vacation pay of` 60_000 `over` 6 `years, the employee having worked` 10 `years`) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2021 `of` 10_000, `a share in the tax year` 2022 `of` 10_000, `a share in the tax year` 2023 `of` 10_000, `a share in the tax year` 2024 `of` 10_000, `a share in the tax year` 2025 `of` 10_000, `a share in the tax year` 2026 `of` 10_000
-- Seven years: over the six. Nought years: not a period. Three years for an employee who worked two: over the years of his work.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`vacation pay of` 60_000 `over` 7 `years, the employee having worked` 10 `years`) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` BECAUSE "section 8(c)(2) lets the period run for at most six tax years ending in the year of receipt and at most the years of the employee's work, and here the number chosen is outside that"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`vacation pay of` 60_000 `over` 0 `years, the employee having worked` 10 `years`) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` BECAUSE "section 8(c)(2) lets the period run for at most six tax years ending in the year of receipt and at most the years of the employee's work, and here the number chosen is outside that"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`vacation pay of` 60_000 `over` 3 `years, the employee having worked` 2 `years`) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` BECAUSE "section 8(c)(2) lets the period run for at most six tax years ending in the year of receipt and at most the years of the employee's work, and here the number chosen is outside that"
-- Over exactly the two years he worked: 30,000 in each of 2025 and 2026.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`vacation pay of` 60_000 `over` 2 `years, the employee having worked` 2 `years`) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2025 `of` 30_000, `a share in the tax year` 2026 `of` 30_000

§§ `Paragraph (3): a grant or a commutation of an annuity`
-- Working years 2015 to 2020, received in 2020: the six tax years 2015 to 2020 are all working years: 120,000 / 6 = 20,000 a year.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2015 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2016 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2017 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2018 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2019 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2020 `of` 20_000
-- Working years 2010 to 2020 (11 years): only the six ending in 2020 count on both readings: 2015 to 2020, 20,000 each.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2015 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2016 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2017 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2018 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2019 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2020 `of` 20_000
-- Working years 2010 to 2018, received in 2020: the six tax years are 2015 to 2020. Only the working years inside: 2015 to 2018, 30,000 each.
-- The last six working years, wherever they fall: 2013 to 2018, 20,000 each. The readings part: declined by default.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `only the working years inside the six tax years count` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2015 `of` 30_000, `a share in the tax year` 2016 `of` 30_000, `a share in the tax year` 2017 `of` 30_000, `a share in the tax year` 2018 `of` 30_000
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the last six working years count, wherever they fall` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2013 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2014 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2015 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2016 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2017 `of` 20_000, `a share in the tax year` 2018 `of` 20_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` BECAUSE "section 8(c)(3) does not say which working years count when they end before the year of receipt, and here it changes the answer"
-- Working years 2010 only, received in 2020: inside the six there is none; the last six working years are [2010]: 120,000 in 2010, or nothing to spread over.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2010)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `only the working years inside the six tax years count` BECAUSE "section 8(c)(3) spreads the grant over the working years it is paid for, and none was given that falls where the section reaches"
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2010)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the last six working years count, wherever they fall` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2010 `of` 120_000
-- Fewer than six working years, all inside the window (2019, 2020): two parts of 60,000 on every reading, so the default answers.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2019, 2020)) `received in` 2020 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2019 `of` 60_000, `a share in the tax year` 2020 `of` 60_000
-- A period the Director allowed, including future years: 2026, 2027, 2028: 40,000 each.
#ASSERT `s 8(c) — where is regarded as received` (`a grant of` 120_000 `for the working years` (LIST 2015, 2016) `with a period allowed by the Director of` (LIST 2026, 2027, 2028)) `received in` 2026 `at a request:` TRUE `, reading an older difference as` `the default older reading` `and working years outside the six as` `the default working-years reading` EQUALS LIST `a share in the tax year` 2026 `of` 40_000, `a share in the tax year` 2027 `of` 40_000, `a share in the tax year` 2028 `of` 40_000
